# Copy of what `make dev-keys` generates, for reference. Do not fill this file
# in and rename it: run `make dev-keys`, which writes a real key pair to a
# git-ignored .env that docker-compose.yml reads.
#
# The pair is per developer and per machine. Nothing outside a local
# `docker compose` stack reads it: the test suite generates its own keys in
# memory, and CI never runs Compose.
#
# IDENTITY_JWT_PRIVATE_KEY is a PKCS#8 RSA private key in PEM form, held only
# by the process that mints tokens. A multi-line value has to be double-quoted
# for Compose to read it whole.
IDENTITY_JWT_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----
...
-----END PRIVATE KEY-----
"
# The key id stamped into every token's `kid` header, so a verifier holding
# several keys knows which one to check the signature with.
IDENTITY_JWT_KEY_ID=local-dev
# A JSON object mapping key id to PEM public key, read by every service that
# verifies. It is a set rather than a single key so a rotation can hold the
# outgoing and the incoming key at once. Single-quoted: the \n escapes are
# part of the JSON and must survive as two characters.
IDENTITY_JWT_PUBLIC_KEYS='{"local-dev":"-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\n...\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----\n"}'
